WEBVTT

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:21.510
You're certainly up and running early.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:22.510
Well, yeah.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:25.830
I need to start looking good again soon.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.410
Have you decided on a return race?

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.670
The Takarazuka Kinen.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.980
I'm gonna win this time.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.510
It'll be my pleasure to 
shatter that confidence.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.140
I'll be going on ahead, then.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.520
I just said I was going to go on ahead!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.740
Honestly...

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.650
Teio-sama certainly seems 
to enjoy her running.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.360
That's just who she is.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:18.720
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:18.720
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:30.520
Episode 9

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.500
Very nice. That was your best time yet.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.620
Really?! Time for another one, then!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.040
Whoa. You sure you're not overdoing it?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.390
Can't help it! I just wanna run so bad!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.020
Looks like our ex-leader is really fired up.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.450
And here I thought I was 
gonna be leader next.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:49.270
Vodka, Scarlet...

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.520
<b>I am the leader</b>

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.200
It's me, your new leader... Golshi-chan.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:00.200
Someone else is feeling motivated, too.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.910
Okay, here I go!

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:06.900
Ready?

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.160
Go!

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.250
<i>I can finally... finally race with McQueen!</i>

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.300
<i>The Classics series is upon us!</i>

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.640
<i>This season, it looks like 
a lot of attention will be</i>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.610
<i>focused on Satsuki winner Narita Taishin!</i>

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.480
Hey, Rice!

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:29.060
<i>There's also Winning Ticket, who's shown
a remarkable focus on the Derby.</i>

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:29.060
Teio-san?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.260
Care for one?

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:36.400
<b>Team
Mimosa
Recruiting Members!!</b>

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.280
<i>And one can hardly ignore the 
looming presence of Biwa Hayahide!</i>

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.310
Oh, I bet you don't eat bread, though!

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.560
Actually, I do, with breakfast.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.120
<i>The three of them are shaping up to be the 
new heroines of this season of racing!</i>

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.400
I see.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.100
Congrats again on the Tennoushou. 
You were really amazing!

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:44.210
<i>So much that I'm sure I don't 
have to tell you they've</i>

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:42.060
Thank you...

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.870
But I'm gonna avenge McQueen.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.230
So be ready to race me some day!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.280
<i>become collectively known as BNW.</i>

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.280
See ya!

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:54.380
<i>And for today's program, I want to 
get up close and personal with BNW!</i>

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.640
We've... already raced before, though.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.750
The horse girls are steadily making 
their way around the track,

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.760
and Narita Taishin is 
currently in third place,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.280
with two competitors in front of her.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.760
<i>We're down to the last 400 meters now.</i>

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.560
<i>And Winning Ticket is moving up!</i>

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.470
<i>Right behind her is Biwa Hayahide!</i>

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.760
<i>Narita Taishin has joined them!</i>

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.770
And it looks like BNW has 
collectively made their move!

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.690
<i>The Derby! The Derby I've 
always dreamed about!</i>

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.770
<i>I may have lost the Satsukishou, 
but this is where I win!</i>

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.660
<i>I can do this! I can come out on top!</i>

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.440
Winning Ticket in the lead!

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:31.260
And Winning Ticket finishes first!

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.790
<b>Japanese Derby</b>

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.410
Biwa Hayahide and Narita Taishin 
in second and third place!

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.790
It looks like BNW are just too strong!

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.800
<i>The Derby goes to Winning Ticket!</i>

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:43.050
<i>Ticket! Ticket! Ticket! {repeat as necessary}</i>

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:53.310
Ticket! Ticket! Ticket! {repeat as necessary}

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.570
W-Wow...

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.190
The race was practically 
between the three of them.

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.190
We've got some more tough competition.

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:02.940
So they're BNW.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.030
They're BNW?!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.750
Not too bad!

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.280
They truly seem to
posses incredible talent.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.550
But so do we.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.990
I did it!

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.460
Ikuno Dictus comes in second 
place at the Yasuda Kinen!

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:23.920
<b>Ikuno Dictus</b>

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:23.920
Congrats, Ikuno!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.330
I would have preferred to have won, but...

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:29.290
A second place finish in 
the G1 is still awesome!

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:30.930
Is your next race set already?

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:32.630
The Takarazuka Kinen.

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.700
Next time, you're gonna win a G1 race!

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.690
Yes. I intend to make up for this loss.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:41.310
I've heard Mejiro McQueen and Tokai Teio 
will be running in the Takarazuka Kinen.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.270
Teio's finally making her return.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:45.490
Well, duh! This is Teio we're talking about!

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.200
Why are <i>you</i> acting so proud?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.360
This time we're gonna beat Spica!

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.290
Right!

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.250
Me too! I wanna race, too!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:56.210
The next race you're eligible for, 
Turbo-san, is the Tanabata Sho.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.670
Is that in the G1?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.080
It's in the G3.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.590
That smells nice.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.200
Ow!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.310
Good day, Palmer.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.470
Hey, McQueen. What's up?

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.370
I never see you around this part of campus.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.710
I'm just here for a change of clothes. 
Then I'll be on my way back to the dorms.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:23.100
Is something going on with you?
 Your nose is very red.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:24.610
Uh, it's nothing!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.110
I see.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.280
I'm afraid I can't allow you to 
win a second Takarazuka Kinen.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.370
Well, I'm not giving up without a fight!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.500
I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.120
If you'll excuse me.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.000
I'm gonna ultim-outrun her!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.960
<i>Two years ago, it was Mejiro Ryan.</i>

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.200
<i>Last year, it was Mejiro Palmer.</i>

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.260
<i>This time, I will be winning.</i>

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.010
Another long day!

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.820
But I've gotta stay on my toes!

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:56.330
Okay, let's do this!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.020
Teio...

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.620
P-Prez...

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.030
How are you feeling?

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.650
Uh... I'm sorry!

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.560
Why are you apologizing?

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:16.990
Well... I've been avoiding you, Prez.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.370
I noticed.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.500
I guess so.

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:26.360
I wasn't sure why I was running.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.040
And I was so anxious.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:32.300
I didn't want you to see me
 when I was like that.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.300
<b>Aim to be an undefeated Triple Crown horse girl!</b>

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.300
I felt guilty.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:37.800
I see.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:38.910
Yeah.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:44.640
But now I have someone who I want 
to look good for as much as you!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.310
As much as me, eh?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.130
Are you jealous?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.500
This is your first race 
in six months, isn't it?

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.360
Yeah. I'm gonna make sure it's a good one.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.420
I want everyone to see, "This is Tokai Teio!"

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.870
Maybe then, instead of chasing you,

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.960
I can be the kind of horse girl who 
can stand next to you as an equal.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.380
And then one day, maybe even surpass you.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:14.610
So the Takarazuka Kinen is going 
to my first step towards that.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.800
Teio...

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:19.750
So be sure to watch me run, Prez!

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.760
Right, I'll be looking forward to it.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:29.970
Back in action, huh?

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.750
I'd expect nothing less of Tokai Teio!

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.180
Of course I'm back, Double Turbo.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.950
It's Twin Turbo! Quit getting it wrong!

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.810
Sorry, sorry!

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:41.250
So did you need something?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.540
I just wanted to let you know 
I'm gonna win the Tanabata Sho!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:45.530
Okay...

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.060
And then I'm gonna come challenge you!

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.470
So next time, we're gonna race!

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.950
Sure, okay.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:53.900
Next time, then.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:57.890
Yeah! It's a promise!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:00.570
What are you doing, Turbo-san?

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.440
Ikuno?!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.430
You can't be bothering Teio-san.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:04.940
I'm not bothering her!

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.960
Come along, now.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.800
Let me go!

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.660
Sorry about that. She doesn't 
mean to cause any trouble.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.340
Ikuno, how are you even doing this?!

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.770
She's just got brain problems.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:13.190
See ya!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:16.820
I wasn't done talking!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.200
Okay, let's do this!

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.200
Let go!

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.500
There we go.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:33.710
<b>Win against McQueen at the Takarazuka Kinen!</b>

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:43.220
Well?

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.030
You're definitely making progress.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:46.100
Keep it up!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:51.110
Oh, damn!

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.110
I'm gonna go again, Trainer!

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.850
All right, go for it!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.740
Okay.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.870
Ready...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:04.780
Go!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:07.920
Awesome!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.500
Yeah!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.810
<i>My legs feel so light.</i>

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.010
<i>My whole body wants to move forward!</i>

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:37.880
<i>No matter how many times I fall,
 I can always dream again!</i>

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:41.950
<i>And this time it's about 
my race with McQueen!</i>

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.490
<i>I want to make sure to win—</i>

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:12.980
Teio!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.980
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.980
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:20.950
It's a fracture.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.950
I see.

00:11:25.310 --> 00:11:29.150
<i>Sorry, McQueen. I'm starting 
over from the beginning again.</i>

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.770
<i>So when will I be able to race?</i>

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.920
This is your third fracture.

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.750
There's a chance it's become recurrent.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.760
The fracture itself should heal,

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:43.680
but it's hard to say whether you'll ever 
be able to run in the same fashion again.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:46.930
You've got about a 70% chance of recovery.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:53.900
It's unfortunate, but continuing 
to race is something I can't—

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.310
It's okay, seriously!

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:59.400
I'll heal! I've done it plenty before, right?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.440
Teio...

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.820
Come on, quit it with that look!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.570
I'm gonna run again! I know it!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.760
It'll be just fine!

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:19.300
I guess my race against McQueen at 
the Takarazuka Kinen is on hold.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.590
I was really looking forward to it, too.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:24.260
Teio, listen...

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.710
I'm counting on you for another 
recovery regimen, Trainer.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:28.020
Sorry.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.980
What're you apologizing for? I'm fine.

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:33.840
I mean it.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.240
<b>BREAKING</b>

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.240
<b>TOKAI TEIO</b>

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.240
<b>THIRD FRACTURE</b>

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.780
<b>Takarazuka Kinen</b>

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.780
<b>Hanshin Racecourse</b>

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:49.140
<b>It's gonna be hard for her to make a comeback...</b>

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:50.790
<b>Thank you for everything</b>

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.330
<b>Get all the rest that you need</b>

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.790
<b>Thank you for the memories,
\hTokai Teio</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.790
<b>Temporarily
Closed</b>

00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:04.550
Kita-chan...

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.340
Teio-san will be okay.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.810
<b>BREAKING</b>

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.810
<b>TOKAI TEIO</b>

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.810
<b>THIRD FRACTURE</b>

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.910
Teio...

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.640
Teio will be back!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.290
I know she will!

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.120
Because she's Tokai Teio!

00:13:36.150 --> 00:13:37.380
Turbo...

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.350
Is there anything we can do for her?

00:13:40.350 --> 00:13:41.610
Give her a watermelon!

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:44.090
Gifts, then? Anything else?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.590
Write her a letter!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.240
Words of encouragement, you mean. I see.

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.240
Teio...

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:48.980
Anything else?

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.480
<i>Palmer begins to fall behind!</i>

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.510
<i>And then, from the outside, 
McQueen is moving up on the outside!</i>

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:08.370
<i>And behind her is Ikuno Dictus!</i>

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.740
<i>But McQueen, she's maintaining her lead!</i>

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.240
<i>And she passes the goal while in first place!</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.240
<b>Takarazuka Kinen</b>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.240
<b>Takarazuka Kinen</b>

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.120
<i>Wow, McQueen was really amazing out there!</i>

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:20.320
<i>Yes, this is her first victory at the 
Takarazuka Kinen. She's bound to be pleased.</i>

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:25.410
<i>She was originally scheduled to 
 race against Tokai Teio.</i>

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:28.050
<i>This is the third time she's 
broken her leg, right?</i>

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:31.510
<b>MCQUEEN TAKES THE TAKARAZUKA!</b>

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.510
<i>From what I hear, there's a good 
chance she may have to exit—</i>

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.080
I don't care what anyone else says.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.630
And there's no point in getting mopey.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.310
Teio-san?!

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.730
Hey! Good to see you all again.

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:52.530
McQueen, congrats on the Takarazuka Kinen!

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:53.860
Teio...

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.920
Are you seriously okay?

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:59.610
I got released last week, 
but I've been bored out of my mind!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.180
So I came to watch you all train.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.760
What's wrong, Gold Ship?!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:10.700
The news wouldn't shut up about you 
not being able to make a comeback!

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:12.800
So I'm just so happy!

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.810
I'm okay!

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:19.270
Trust me, you break your leg three times, 
and you start to get a feel for how bad it is.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.690
This is so great, Teio-san!

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:24.990
If you need to do rehab, I've got 
your back! Anything you need!

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.170
Continuing to race is something I can't—

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.840
Yeah. Thanks, guys.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.740
So, that said...

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:37.120
Sitting around is gonna just make me anxious,

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.140
so starting today, I'll be supporting 
you all as team leader again!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:43.250
<b>I am the leader</b>

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.250
If you need any shopping done
or anything, let me know!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.810
Your reign only lasted a few days, huh?

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:45.710
Shut it.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.450
You're sure that's all right?

00:15:47.450 --> 00:15:48.250
You bet!

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.500
Leave it to me!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.220
<b>S.S. Golshi #2</b>

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:56.350
Let's see, I got that, and that...

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:00.840
So that leaves compresses, 
supplements, protein, and...

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:01.470
Hey, it's Tokai Teio!

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.120
Hello there.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:04.230
Hello there!

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:06.160
Um, Teio-san...

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.020
We used to root for you.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.090
You had a really great run.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:14.840
Thank you for everything.

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:15.990
You too, Kanna.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.700
Good luck, Teio-san!

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.240
Uh... Right.

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.970
You'll have to excuse us.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.330
Bye-bye!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:23.500
Bye-bye.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:29.200
"Used to root for you," huh?

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:32.270
Okay, back to shopping.

00:16:32.270 --> 00:16:34.800
Honey, honey, honey,

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.740
honey...

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.230
Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! {repeat as necessary}

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:59.790
Sweets! Sweets! Sweets! {repeat as necessary}

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:03.200
Why?! Why am I so slow?!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:06.210
Hurry it up! We're going on ahead!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.290
Wait up!

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:08.460
Guys!

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.590
Hey, listen!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.880
Don't leave me behind!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.920
Guys!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:39.910
Sweets, sweets, sweets...

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.910
Is something wrong?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.160
Well, it's just...

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:44.990
What do you think, McQueen?

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:55.920
This is her third fracture.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:59.140
Do you think Teio will be able 
to run again like she used to?

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:03.320
She believes she can.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.900
And I must simply believe in her.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.710
I see.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:15.070
You shouldn't be so hard on yourself. 
It's only going to make Teio more anxious.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:18.150
Right... sorry.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.400
Teio, you got a second?

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:39.800
What's up?

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:42.320
Well, y'know...

00:18:42.320 --> 00:18:45.250
And hey, when are you gonna 
have my comeback plan ready?

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.940
I'm getting tired of waiting!

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:49.810
Yeah, you're right. Sorry.

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:52.100
Seriously, quit apologizing!

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.310
Hey, there you are.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.520
Sup.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.390
What's up, guys? Did you go shopping?

00:18:57.390 --> 00:18:58.240
Yeah!

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:01.020
Teio-san, this is perfect timing!

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.910
Ta-dah! We're making you a nutrition drink!

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:10.090
We were wondering if our special drink 
is what helped you bounce back last time.

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:10.890
Right?

00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:12.790
Oh... you were?

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.090
Please drink it so you'll feel better sooner!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:16.390
Let's see, first...

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:19.640
It's gotta have milk, right? 
She needs her calcium!

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.260
What about garlic, for stamina?

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.030
That's still rejected from last time!

00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:25.130
Let's put some carrots in! They're delicious!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.240
How about dried sardines?

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:28.710
We're not just putting 
in <i>anything</i> for calcium!

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.120
Thanks, guys.

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:33.350
I bet I'll be able to run again in no time.

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:38.030
Maybe even faster than before!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.640
Hey, don't expect too much!

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:40.890
Please get well soon!

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.660
Yeah, hurry it up already!

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:55.070
<i>It's hard to say whether you'll ever be 
able to run in the same fashion again.</i>

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:57.810
<i>There's a good chance she 
may have to exit the—</i>

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:00.690
<i>Teio-san, we used to root for you.</i>

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.450
Oh, Teio.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:16.250
Hey, McQueen. Doing some late secret training?

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:16.940
Yes.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.070
It'd be a sorry state of affairs 
if I wasn't prepared for when

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:21.440
my rival returns to racing.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:23.380
Teio!

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:26.230
Could you call my time?

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.830
You sure you want your rival 
to have that kind of intel?

00:20:30.980 --> 00:20:34.830
Get a good look at how I run.

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:40.640
I'll always be waiting up ahead.

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:47.970
Waiting for you.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.130
Ready...

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:53.580
Go!

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.660
<i>Wow... she's so fast.</i>

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.110
<i>Like she's flying.</i>

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:50.780
<i>It's so beautiful.</i>

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:05.370
I see. I get it now.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:10.840
Teio? How was that?

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:17.750
I'm never...

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:21.120
gonna be able to run like that again.

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:24.970
What was that? I didn't hear you!

00:22:24.970 --> 00:22:26.490
What was my time?

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:29.490
Teio! Say, Teio!

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:33.060
What was my time?!

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:33.480
I'm so sorry, McQueen.

00:22:33.480 --> 00:22:35.310
Teio, are you listening?
